Idea 2 — 

Temp folder (Delete → Copy → Move, linear) + alert on failure + manual rerun. Best suited for SHIR, since most SHIR failures (machine off, VPN down, network drop) genuinely need a human to fix the underlying infrastructure, no amount of automatic retrying fixes a machine that's powered off. So a simple, observable, manually-recoverable design is the right trade-off there, not a limitation, a deliberate choice given what actually breaks.

